ine, the failure of a single flow does not cause other parallel flows to fail. In a continuous pipeline, an expectation failure stops the flow, all dependent flows, and the pipeline emits a message explaining why it stopped.\nL231: \nL232: For more control over workflow orchestration when a validation fails, split the validation and downstream work into separate pipelines and coordinate them with control flow between the pipeline tasks. See cite20†Validation tables and pipeline control flow .\n"
